  "body": "What changed:\n- The 50 s default-cap pin moves to its own test binary, `import_step_guard_default_cap`.\n- The earlier commit stays: the two capped pins use a 120 s hang barrier.\n- Product code is unchanged.\n\nCause: truck tessellates on rayon's global pool. The default-cap import holds pool workers for about 50 s. Cheap pins in the same process queue behind it. Alone, the may-jump pin takes 0.02 s. With the heavy pin in the same process, it finished after 79 s. Under CPU load, the old 30 s barrier failed. The refusal itself depends only on the input.\n\nTested:\n- `import_step_guard` (5 tests) in 30 parallel runs, with the heavy binary running at the same time: all green, 0.9 s each.\n- `import_step_guard_default_cap`: green.\n- clippy `-D warnings` on both test targets: clean.\n\nNot exercised: the Linux runner. One earlier report of an assertion failure (not the barrier) on the may-jump pin did not reproduce here. See `docs/decisions/1605-import-guard-flake.md`.\n\nChangelog: none\nEffort: medium (after one escalation from low)\n\nFixes #1605\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
